---
title: Install Dependencies and Run the App
description: Install Node.js dependencies with Yarn and start Vera in development mode.
---

# Install Dependencies and Run the App

## 1. Install dependencies

From the project root, run:

```bash
yarn install
```

Yarn reads `yarn.lock` and installs the exact dependency versions used by the project. This only needs to be done once (or whenever dependencies change).

> **Note:** The setup script ran this command for you automatically. You only need to re-run it if you add or update packages.

---

## 2. Start the application in development mode

```bash
yarn dev
```

This single command starts two servers concurrently:

| Server | URL | Description |
|--------|-----|-------------|
| **Frontend** (Vite) | [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) | React application with hot-module replacement |
| **Backend** (Express) | [http://localhost:3345](http://localhost:3345) | API server that issues Video API tokens |

The terminal output will confirm both servers are running:

```
[frontend] VITE ready in Xms ➜  Local: http://localhost:5173/
[backend]  Server listening on port 3345
```

---

## 3. Open the app in your browser

Navigate to [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173).

You should see the Vera landing page where you can type a room name and join a video call.

---

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| `Error: VONAGE_APP_ID is not set` | Open `backend/.env` and make sure `VONAGE_APP_ID` is filled in correctly. |
| `Error: VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY is not set` | Make sure the full private key (including header/footer lines) is present in `backend/.env`. |
| Port already in use | Another process is using port 3345 or 5173. Stop it or change the port in `vcrBuild.env.sh` (`API_URL`) and `backend/.env`. |
| Camera / microphone not working | The browser requires a secure context (HTTPS or `localhost`). Make sure you are opening `http://localhost:5173`, not a different hostname. |

---

## What's next?

Now that the application is running locally, you can explore the codebase and customise it for your use case:

- **Frontend feature flags** – edit [`vcrBuild.env.sh`](../../../vcrBuild.env.sh) to toggle chat, archiving, captions, and more.
- **UI theming** – edit `designTokens.json` and run `yarn sync:theme-tokens` to update the colour palette.
- **Storybook** – run `yarn storybook` to browse and develop UI components in isolation.
- **Tests** – run `yarn test` to execute the full unit-test suite.

For the full list of available options see the [README](../../../README.md).
